            <ArticleTitle>Effect of diltiazem, nifedipine and verapamil on the antinociceptive action of acetylsalicylic acid in mice.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>121-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>1. Diltiazem, verapamil and nifedipine produced a dose-dependent analgesic response in mice. 2. A fixed oral dose of acetylsalicylic acid increased this analgesic response. 3. Analgesia was maintained when mice were treated chronically with calcium channel blockers alone or when combined with aspirin.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
